    {
     "author": {
      "accountId": "5cdf0dfb3b428d0dcd7c7c4d",
      "accountType": "atlassian",
      "active": false,
      "avatarUrls": {
       "16x16": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "24x24": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "32x32": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png",
       "48x48": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/default/default-avatar.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Former user",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5cdf0dfb3b428d0dcd7c7c4d",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I wonder if we're conflating two ideas here? To me an audit is about validation, e.g. by recalculating checksums and verifying that they match. I think it would be great if we could do that as part of the export/import and have that in a field in addition to those above (it could just be a boolean value or \"checksum matches: true\") but I want to make sure that that's what you mean.</p>\n\n<p>If validating checksums is out of scope, then I think what <a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a> suggests above is fine (it should be easy to parse, which that would be, and I can't immediately think of any other elements I'd want)--but I wouldn't call it an audit log.</p>",
     "created": "26/Sep/16 9:15 PM",
     "id": "17636",
     "jsdPublic": true,
